From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Correct configured pkg-config library and include paths

The CMake install puts headers in include/libdxfrw, not libdxfrw1, and a
literal vertical bar in libdir makes downstream linking fail. Keep the
upstream library, converter, exports and all build targets unchanged.
Downstream packaging correction for 1.0.1; no upstream write performed.

--- a/libdxfrw.pc.in
+++ b/libdxfrw.pc.in
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
 prefix=${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
 exec_prefix=${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}
-libdir=|${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR}
+libdir=${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_LIBDIR}
 includedir=${CMAKE_INSTALL_FULL_INCLUDEDIR}
@@ -7,4 +7,4 @@
 Description: c++ library to read/write dxf files in binary and ascii form
 Version: ${PROJECT_VERSION}
 Libs: -L${libdir} -ldxfrw
-Cflags: -I${includedir}/libdxfrw${PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR}
+Cflags: -I${includedir}/libdxfrw
